{
  "type": "doc",
  "content": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "After finding container access records, knowing which files were read and what values appeared makes the work easier to understand."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "I inspected a test Pod briefly, then tried "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "replaying it in Pod Session Recordings"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ". Linking connection records to actual terminal screens was the most striking part."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "attrs": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Checking Cluster Recording Settings"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "In acp-kac-lab Logging Options, "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Pod Session Recording was On"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ", and Request Audit was enabled too, allowing shell requests and recordings to be reviewed together."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/pod-session-recording/01.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 1. Pod Session Recording and Request Audit enabled on the cluster.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 1. Pod Session Recording and Request Audit enabled on the cluster."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "I prepared a dedicated Pod named "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "ep45-session-demo"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " with a fictional status file containing service, environment, and status, without production data."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "In QueryPie I created "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Orders Lab Pod Inspector"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " with a policy allowing Pod reads in orders-lab and this test Pod’s "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "pods/exec"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " operations, and assigned it to the inspection test account."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/pod-session-recording/02.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 2. Dedicated policy for viewing the test Pod and entering its shell.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 2. Dedicated policy for viewing the test Pod and entering its shell."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "attrs": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Performing a Familiar Pod Inspection"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "With the test account, I opened QueryPie’s "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Web Client"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " and selected ep45-session-demo in orders-lab. Pod Running and diagnostics Ready were shown; I clicked "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Shell"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " to connect."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/pod-session-recording/03.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 3. Pod/container healthy; opening Shell.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 3. Pod/container healthy; opening Shell."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "id and hostname returned UID/GID 10001 and ep45-session-demo. Then I ran "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "cat /lab/health.txt"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " to read the file: service orders-demo, environment lab, status "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "READY"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "I printed EP45_POD_CHECK_COMPLETE as a recognizable marker for replay, then exited normally."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/pod-session-recording/04.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 4. Account, hostname, status file, and completion marker in the container.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 4. Account, hostname, status file, and completion marker in the container."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "attrs": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Opening Recordings After the Work"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "I opened the administrator’s "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Audit → Kubernetes → Pod Session Recordings"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " and found Demo Approver’s session on acp-kac-lab with Orders Lab Pod Inspector."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The target was "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "the session starting at 12:54:50"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ". User, role, and start time made it easy to find."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/pod-session-recording/05.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 5. Finding the recording by user and time.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 5. Finding the recording by user and time."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "attrs": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Commands and Their Output Reappear"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Clicking the timestamp opened "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Pod Session Record"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " with user, start, source, and command above Replay. The source was Web Client and shell sh."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Play showed the entered commands in order, including "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "id output, Pod name, and READY in the status file"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ", showing both actions and the information used to judge the state."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/pod-session-recording/06.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 6. Replay shows the actual inspection commands and file contents.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 6. Replay shows the actual inspection commands and file contents."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The end retained the completion marker and exit. Playback lasted about 14 seconds, and seeking could restart from a chosen point."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/pod-session-recording/07.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 7. Completion marker and shell exit remain in the recording.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 7. Completion marker and shell exit remain in the recording."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "This would help handovers: administrators can see the same sequence and results rather than rely on a verbal account."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "attrs": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Audit Links Directly to the Recording"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Request Audit"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " also contained shell start at 12:54:50 and exit at 12:55:04. The exit recorded "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Success, ALLOW"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ", exit code 0, and duration 13.82 seconds."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Details showed user, role, orders-lab, pods/exec, and ep45-session-demo. The "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Session Recording"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " link reopened the same recording."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/pod-session-recording/08.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 8. Successful exit, target, and audit link to the same recording.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 8. Successful exit, target, and audit link to the same recording."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "What stood out was "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "the connection between access management and evidence of actual work"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ". After identifying who entered, I could follow what they did and saw."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "For adoption evaluation, concrete operational evidence matters: user, role, commands, outputs, and successful exit could be reviewed as one task."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "This lab used QueryPie Community 11.6.7 Web Client and K3s 1.36.6. User, Pod, and file were for testing; the temporary inspection role was revoked afterward."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Reference: "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "link",
              "attrs": {
                "href": "https://docs.querypie.com/ko/administrator-manual/audit/kubernetes-logs/pod-session-recordings",
                "target": "_blank",
                "rel": "noopener noreferrer nofollow",
                "class": null,
                "title": null
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "QueryPie Pod Session Recordings guide"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
